+/**
+ * Plays progressive HTTP files over a few parallel range requests when one connection is too slow,
+ * for servers that limit the speed of each connection.
+ *
+ * <p>The source starts as a normal single request. While the player reads, it measures how fast
+ * that connection delivers. Only when it is slower than {@link #SLOW_BYTES_PER_SECOND} does it
+ * switch, at the current byte, to downloading the next chunks in order over up to
+ * {@link #MAX_CONNECTIONS} connections. The player still receives the bytes strictly in order.
+ *
+ * <p>To stay light on the server: chunks start at 1 MB so playback starts quickly, then grow to
+ * 8 MB so a long video needs few requests; only a small window ahead of the player is fetched, so
+ * nothing is requested while the player's buffer is full; a 429 or 503 permanently lowers the
+ * connection count for that host; and a server that ignores ranges, or any repeated failure,
+ * returns this source to a single normal request.
